  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite the second factor using the power of product rule:\n\n$$\n{4}^{8}\\cdot {(4\\cdot 3)}^{7}={4}^{8}\\cdot {4}^{7}\\cdot {3}^{7}\n$$\n\nFinally, we apply the product rule for exponents, and simplify:\n\n$$\n{4}^{8}\\cdot {4}^{7}\\cdot {3}^{7}={4}^{8+7}\\cdot {3}^{7}={4}^{15}\\cdot {3}^{7}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
